# FlowForge Engine

Fault-Tolerant Distributed Workflow Orchestration Platform

FlowForge is a reusable, domain-independent workflow orchestration engine designed to execute long-running dependent workflows under realistic distributed-system failure conditions.

The project is demonstrated through a separate VoltOps reference application for outage-aware electrical maintenance.

## Project Structure

```text
flowforge-engine/
├── docs/
│   ├── 01-problem-discovery.md
│   ├── 02-architecture-proposal.md
│   ├── 03-data-model-proposal.md
│   ├── 04-state-machine-proposal.md
│   ├── 05-failure-analysis.md
│   └── 06-technology-decisions.md
├── flowforge-engine/
├── voltops-reference/
├── docker-compose.yml
└── pom.xml
```

## Week 1 Status

Week 1 is a discovery and system-design phase. Production workflow-execution logic is intentionally not implemented yet.

### Goals

- Define the problem and consistency requirements.
- Propose the system architecture.
- Propose the data model and state machines.
- Analyze distributed failure scenarios.
- Compare key technology and architecture alternatives.
- Bootstrap the repository and development environment.

## Technology

- Java 21
- Spring Boot
- Maven
- PostgreSQL
- Docker Compose

## Repository Boundary

`flowforge-engine` contains only domain-independent workflow orchestration concepts.

`voltops-reference` contains electrical-maintenance business concepts and consumes FlowForge as a client/library.

## Development

The repository is currently being bootstrapped for Week 1 design review. Implementation stages will follow after the design review.
